one"},{"surface":"வாய்","parts":[{"text":"வாய்","lemma":"வாய்","gloss":"mouth"}],"gloss":"mouth"},{"surface":"சிவந்து","parts":[{"text":"சிவந்து","lemma":"சிவ","gloss":"having become red"}],"gloss":"having become red"},{"surface":"மேல்","parts":[{"text":"மேல்","lemma":"மேல்","gloss":"upon"}],"gloss":"upon"},{"surface":"வருக","parts":[{"text":"வருக","lemma":"வா","gloss":"may you come"}],"gloss":"may you come"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"சிறுகண்","parts":[{"text":"சிறு","lemma":"சிறு","gloss":"small"},{"text":"கண்","lemma":"கண்","gloss":"eye"}],"gloss":"small-eyed"},{"surface":"யானை","parts":[{"text":"யானை","lemma":"யானை","gloss":"elephant"}],"gloss":"elephant"},{"surface":"வேந்து","parts":[{"text":"வேந்து","lemma":"வேந்து","gloss":"king"}],"gloss":"king"},{"surface":"விழுமுறவே","parts":[{"text":"விழுமுறவே","lemma":"விழுமமுறு","gloss":"indeed to suffer distress"}],"gloss":"indeed to suffer distress"}]}],"literal":"Praising with toddy, praising with toddy, / in the un-swept courtyard dense with the forest, / he who sleeps in the drowsiness of morning intoxication, / he is our lord, we are his bards. / For the guest who came yesterday, / he pledged his old sword with an iron hilt; today, / taking this black-stemmed small lute as pledge, / without saying 'he has nothing to give', you too, / so that your wife with a creeper-like waist wears shining jewels, / and we, with vessels containing toddy, sway in joy, / go, and may you return with your mouth reddened / by the king of small-eyed elephants suffering distress!","translation":"Praising with toddy, praising with toddy, in the un-swept courtyard surrounded by dense forest, he sleeps in the drowsiness of morning intoxication. He is our lord, and we are his bards. For the guest who arrived yesterday, he pledged his old sword with an iron hilt. Today, taking this black-stemmed small lute as collateral, do not say 'he has nothing to give.' Go, so that your wife with a creeper-like waist may wear shining jewels, and we, with vessels of toddy, may sway in joy. May you return with your mouth reddened with rich food and betel, while the enemy king with small-eyed elephants suffers distress!","modern":"கள் குடித்து வாழ்த்தி, கள் குடித்து வாழ்த்தி, காடு சூழ்ந்த பெருக்காத முற்றத்தில், காலையில் உண்ட கள்ளின் மயக்கத்தால் தூங்குகின்றானே, அவன் எமது தலைவன்; நாம் அவனுடைய பாணர்கள். நேற்று வந்த விருந்தினரை உபசரிக்கத் தன் இரும்புக் கைப்பிடி கொண்ட பழைய வாளினை அடகு வைத்தான். இன்று, இந்தக் கரிய தண்டினைக் கொண்ட சிறிய யாழினை அடகு வைத்து உதவி செய்வான். 'கொடுப்பதற்கு அவனிடம் ஏதும் இல்லை' என்று எண்ணாமல் நீயும் செல்வாயாக. கொடி போன்ற இடையைக் கொண்ட உன் மனைவி விளங்கும் அணிகலன்களை அணியவும், கள் நிறைந்த பாத்திரங்களுடன் நாம் மகிழ்ச்சியில் திளைக்கவும், சிறிய கண்களை உடைய யானைகளைக் கொண்ட பகை வேந்தன் துன்பமடையுமாறு, நீ அவனிடம் சென்று வெற்ற வெற்றிலையால் வாய் சிவந்து மீண்டு வருவாயாக!","explanation":"A bard is speaking to another visiting bard, praising the immense generosity of his chief in the Vallāṇ Mullai theme. The chief is currently sleeping off his morning toddy in his rustic, un-swept courtyard surrounded by forest. Though he is poor, his spirit of hospitality is boundless; he pledged his iron-hilted sword to feed yesterday's guests, and today he is ready to pledge his small lute to help the new visitor. The speaker urges the visitor not to hesitate or think the chief has nothing left to give. By going to him, the visitor's wife will receive fine jewels, the bards will feast on toddy, and they will return with mouths reddened by betel, while the enemy king with small-eyed elephants suffers defeat and distress.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.7],[0.7,1.1],[1.1,1.5],[1.5,2.8],[2.8,3.2],[3.2,3.3],[3.3,3.6],[3.6,5.0],[5.0,5.3],[5.43,5.7],[5.75,5.9],[6.0,6.9],[6.9,7.2],[7.2,7.3],[7.3,8.2],[8.2,8.6],[8.6,9.03],[9.47,9.9],[9.9,10.34],[10.34,10.74],[10.74,11.0],[11.0,12.07],[12.13,12.4],[12.4,12.9],[12.9,13.14],[13.2,14.3],[14.3,14.4],[14.4,15.0],[15.0,15.2],[15.2,15.2],[15.2,15.2],[15.2,17.5],